1
00:00:00,785 --> 00:00:04,415
Oh, that is so, so...

2
00:00:05,873 --> 00:00:09,753
I'm sorry, I gotta run. If you
come up with an adjective, text me.

3
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,209
[DOOR CLOSES]

4
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:17,050
(Sheldon:)Inconsiderate. That is the adjective.
Inconsiderate.

5
00:00:18,719 --> 00:00:21,759
(Leonard(exiting the apartment):)You can stare at your board all day,
she's still going to be right.

6
00:00:21,931 --> 00:00:23,561
SHELDON:
I'm not staring, I'm mulling.

7
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:25,474
- Oh, hey, Leonard.
- Hi.

8
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:30,060
[TEASING]
So how's it going?

9
00:00:32,316 --> 00:00:34,446
[IMITATES PENNY]
Pretty good.

10
00:00:34,819 --> 00:00:38,699
Just pretty good? I'd think
you were doing very good.

11
00:00:39,907 --> 00:00:43,827
"Pretty, very." There's really no objective
scale for delineating variations of good.

12
00:00:43,994 --> 00:00:46,124
(Leonard:)Why do you ask?

13
00:00:46,288 --> 00:00:50,128
(Penny:)Well, a little bird told me that
you and Leslie hooked up last night.

14
00:00:51,961 --> 00:00:54,801
- Sheldon!
SHELDON: I'm coming.

15
00:00:54,964 --> 00:00:57,554
So is it serious? Do you like her?

